.claude/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Built _site/ (Netlify publish target) — produced fresh on every deploy.
_site/

# Local downloads of the DATAtourisme regional export (~45 MB, rebuilt daily).
datatourisme-reg-*.csv

# Never public: contributed photo originals (promise to the photographer).
incoming-benedicte/

.env*
*.bak
*.tmp

# Generic photo library copied from the 74 as a baseline — large binaries.
# Remove this rule if the generiques should be version-controlled here.

# Engine byproducts — regenerated on every build.
scripts/__pycache__/
_site/

# reports/ is TRACKED, matching the 74. It holds evidence, not byproducts:
# gates fail closed when their file is absent, so ignoring the directory made
# a gate green on a developer's machine go red in CI, where reports/ was never
# checked out. That is exactly how this repo's first CI run died — on
# reports/featured-placements-baseline.md, a file an allowlist of four
# negations did not happen to name. Ignore the transient work artifacts by
# name instead; anything a gate reads is committed by default.
reports/leak-work-*.json
reports/leak-out-*.json
reports/__pycache__/
